4. Variant calling using minimap2, samtools & PEPPER (through docker)
conda activate align_tools

Previous guide from KEMRI training (October 2024, 2. Evaluate the pipeline command and results2.docx) used FASTQ mannually merged from fastq_pass folder, including DCS removal.
I skip this process and used fastqs generated by GHRU-mod (I modified the pipeline for including fastq copy to /fastqs folder in the output folder).

Previous KEMRI training guide (October 2024, 2. Evaluate the pipeline command and the results.2.docx) used basecalled FASTQs manually merged from the /fastq_pass folder, including DCS removal.
I skipped this step and instead used FASTQs stored in /fastqs generated by GHRU-mod (I modified the pipeline to include fastq copy to the /fastqs subdirectory in the output folder).

Because each sample MUST be variant-called with specific bacterial species reference (Ref.) genome, I designed an executable loop for each sample listed in a *csv.




minimap2 -a Kleb.pneuMGH78578.fasta mysample001_only_reads.fastq > aligned_long_reads.sam
samtools view -S -b aligned_long_reads.sam | samtools sort -o sorted_long_reads.bam
samtools index sorted_long_reads.bam
samtools rmdup sorted_long_reads.bam deduplicated.bam
samtools faidx Kleb.pneuMGH78578.fasta
mkdir reference
mv Kleb.pneuMGH78578.fasta Kleb.pneuMGH78578.fasta.fai sorted_long_reads.bam sorted_long_reads.bam.bai reference 

















